WEBVTT

00:00:02.581 --> 00:00:07.970
A live number is gone in a second. Telo Ride now keeps the ride's totals: distance,

00:00:07.970 --> 00:00:09.439
output and energy.

00:00:10.324 --> 00:00:15.310
Each running second adds the speed over thirty-six hundred to distance. An hour at

00:00:15.310 --> 00:00:17.312
thirty is thirty kilometres.

00:00:20.647 --> 00:00:25.687
A paused ride has no running seconds, so its distance and output hold, however long

00:00:25.687 --> 00:00:26.594
the pause.

00:00:30.971 --> 00:00:35.866
Each running second also adds its power over a thousand to the ride's output, in

00:00:35.866 --> 00:00:36.839
kilojoules.

00:00:41.295 --> 00:00:46.450
Energy follows. Two hundred and eight watts for seven hundred and sixty seconds is a

00:00:46.450 --> 00:00:49.021
hundred and fifty-seven kilocalories.

00:00:51.618 --> 00:00:56.691
An unknown value shows as a dash, never a stale number, and distance always shows

00:00:56.691 --> 00:00:57.805
two decimals.

00:01:01.942 --> 00:01:06.863
Three kinds of readouts share these helpers: the class ride's tiles, the race power

00:01:06.863 --> 00:01:09.416
panel and the custom ride's dashboard.

00:01:12.266 --> 00:01:17.233
On the simulated bike, a minute of frames turns into distance, output and energy,

00:01:17.233 --> 00:01:18.208
end to end.

00:01:22.590 --> 00:01:28.534
Still to come: the ride clock ticks the totals in slice 5.1, and Class Ride first

00:01:28.534 --> 00:01:30.155
shows them in 5.2.

00:01:32.913 --> 00:01:37.552
Home doesn't change yet, at any width. The totals wait in the engine for the ride

00:01:37.552 --> 00:01:38.310
screens.

00:01:43.237 --> 00:01:47.758
What the tests prove: twenty new unit tests, one per row of the requirements, and

00:01:47.758 --> 00:01:49.342
every spec still green.

00:01:53.561 --> 00:01:58.164
Telo Ride, from the Telo family, turns a smart bike at home into a game.

00:01:58.509 --> 00:02:03.021
It pairs with the bike over Bluetooth, reads your power and sets resistance for

00:02:03.021 --> 00:02:04.692
every hill and interval.

00:02:05.037 --> 00:02:10.215
Two doors: Race (ride a map against your best-time ghost, bots or people) and

00:02:10.215 --> 00:02:15.663
Classes (ride along to a video, alone or with a group), fed by one progression of

00:02:15.663 --> 00:02:18.653
XP, rider levels, stars and map unlocks.

00:02:18.998 --> 00:02:21.491
A custom workout lives under Profile.
